# What `docker build` is allowed to see (the "build context"). Anything not allowed here
# never leaves your machine, so it can't end up in an image. The image may be public,
# and this folder holds things that must never be: `private/` (the real timetable),
# `vault/` (study notes) and `.env` files (secrets).
#
# Rule 1: deny everything.
*

# Rule 2: allow back only what the image is built from.
!package.json
!pnpm-lock.yaml
!pnpm-workspace.yaml
!tsconfig.base.json
!apps/
!packages/

# Rule 3: inside those folders, still never send these. Installed packages and build
# output are recreated inside the build; tests aren't needed to run the app.
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/coverage
**/.vite
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/*.log
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.test.ts
**/*.test.tsx
**/__snapshots__

# Rule 4: named explicitly even though rule 1 already covers them. Later lines win, so
# these stay out even if someone adds a broader "!" line above by mistake.
private
vault
.env
.env.*
.git
.github
.claude
.claude-flow
.swarm
.code-review-graph
ruvector.db
*.rvf*
docs
deploy
*.txt
.vscode
.idea
